{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault","id":1526391,"title":"Book of Common Magicks released on ST Vault","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-06T00:04:00-08:00","id":1526391,"title":"Book of Common Magicks released on ST Vault","content":"I dropped this on ST Vault about a week back - figured folks might be interested <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/462226/Book-of-Common-Magicks\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Common Magicks - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault</a>\u200b<br /> <br /> It's all the common Effects that used to be in the magic chapter of Mage 1e, 2e, and Revised, but were left out of M20. I've rewritten them, expanded them, updated them to M20 rules and worked hard to keep them in line with material from HDYDT? and Book of Secrets. There's also a few concepts adapted from Mage: the Awakening and added in where appropriate, to flesh out the Spheres. I've also included those Effects specific to the Technocratic Sphere and, as a bonus, added the one-page Sphere summaries like we had back in the 2e era.<br /> <br /> If you want to see my approach, the full-sized preview on the product's page gives the whole Prime Sphere for free.<br /> <br /> It's designed to give a clear understanding of the fundaments of the Spheres. HDYDT? covers some of this ground but goes into more complex cases - there's currently no nuts &amp; bolts overview of the basic Effects for each Sphere, properly fleshed out. A couple of my players asked me to make this and I figured why not stick it on the Vault when done. It's 80 pages and 5 bucks. Thank you if you feel like checking it out - enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T02:20:51-08:00","id":1526393,"title":"","content":"It's on my list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T03:07:33-08:00","id":1526395,"title":"","content":"Already bought it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T03:22:30-08:00","id":1526396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault?p=1526395#post1526395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Already bought it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T11:01:27-08:00","id":1526614,"title":"","content":"You know, I was in the process of planning out a book that did something similar to this. Though the scope was a bit wider, also giving details on conjunctional effects and how they were handled in prior editions, as well as notes on different types of ways the spheres might behave given different paradigms<br /> <br /> But this seems to fit the bill of what the mage community sorely needed for new players, so I hoped when I saw this that there is no longer such a need for what I had considered.<br /> <br /> Though I think there might be a bit of controversy around the additions, such as allowing a mage to absorb quintessence with Prime 1, allowing consecration of Life patterns with Prime 2, and limiting gravity manipulation to Forces 4 and above.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the introduction of temporal sympathy seems unnecessary since sympathetic magic is something true for all casting, as seen in the casting table. In fact, its inclusion would be more confusing for new players who would otherwise not find the concept mentioned in any other source. That a<br /> <br /> These are rather major shifts in how the spheres behave that will certainly lead to a few raised eyebrows. And the fact that these changes are intermixed with previous edition updates and current edition elements without any means for the uninitiated to tell between them makes this a source that I cannot recommend to new players, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> In my plan, I had the idea to source each effect to the editions they came from, and specifically highlight any new things I introduced as new such that the community can decide whether or not to include it without questioning whether it was new to this book or simply from an older book or a better explained version from the current book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-10-2023, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T11:51:30-08:00","id":1526619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault?p=1526614#post1526614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was in the process of planning out a book that did something similar to this. Though the scope was a bit wider, also giving details on conjunctional effects and how they were handled in prior editions, as well as notes on different types of ways the spheres might behave given different paradigms<br /> <br /> But this seems to fit the bill of what the mage community sorely needed for new players, so I hoped when I saw this that there is no longer such a need for what I had considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you - that's exactly the intention with this product and I really do want buyers to see it the same way. I think it would be cool to see something for conjunctional Effects as well - I do have a mad plan to update all the existing published Effects to M20 but that's not a small task!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault?p=1526614#post1526614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I think there might be a bit of controversy around the additions, such as allowing a mage to absorb quintessence with Prime 1, allowing consecration of Life patterns with Prime 2, and limiting gravity manipulation to Forces 4 and above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't additions, though. Absorbing Quintessence with Prime 1 is on <b>M20</b> page 520 and <b>HDYDT?</b> page 42, consecrating Life Patterns with Prime 2 is also on <b>M20 </b>page 520 and <b>HDYDT?</b> page 46, and gravity manipulation isn't limited to Forces 4 and above - see Control Gravity on <b>Book of Common Magicks</b> page 20 for a Forces 2 version. The Forces 4 version is for large-scale Effects, as is normal for Forces 4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault?p=1526614#post1526614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, the introduction of temporal sympathy seems unnecessary since sympathetic magic is something true for all casting, as seen in the casting table. In fact, its inclusion would be more confusing for new players who would otherwise not find the concept mentioned in any other source.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks - I would hope that it just clarifies how sympathy works with temporal scrying as well as spatial scrying and doesn't confuse people, but thanks for raising that point. It's worth keeping in mind for any future products.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault?p=1526614#post1526614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are rather major shifts in how the spheres behave that will certainly lead to a few raised eyebrows. And the fact that these changes are intermixed with previous edition updates and current edition elements without any means for the uninitiated to tell between them makes this a source that I cannot recommend to new players, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> In my plan, I had the idea to source each effect to the editions they came from, and specifically highlight any new things I introduced as new such that the community can decide whether or not to include it without questioning whether it was new to this book or simply from an older book or a better explained version from the current book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as I say, I disagree that most of the above are major shifts or additions but I do appreciate you taking the time to write out your feedback and I do take it in the spirit it's intended. I would hope that newcomers find it useful as I have tried to make it fit closely with M20 rules but of course it's not going to be for everyone. All the same, thank you very much for buying a copy - that is very cool.<br /> <br /> (<b>EDIT:</b> The only stuff that's genuinely new is one Effect in Prime (Obfuscation), taken from something similar in Mage: the Awakening. That's all. A few Effects are inferred from the existing Sphere descriptions: the stuff on fate and destiny in Entropy and the Unseen Aegis Effect in Matter, and I took inspiration from Awakening for some of these. Everything else comes from M20, supplemented by elements from Revised for detail. If folks think it would be helpful, I can update the product with a section that details this.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","user":"Thebian","date":". 12-10-2023, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T13:39:04-08:00","id":1526625,"title":"","content":"For clarity, you probably should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T14:31:06-08:00","id":1526628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault?p=1526619#post1526619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you - that's exactly the intention with this product and I really do want buyers to see it the same way. I think it would be cool to see something for conjunctional Effects as well - I do have a mad plan to update all the existing published Effects to M20 but that's not a small task!<br /> <br /> <br /> Those aren't additions, though. Absorbing Quintessence with Prime 1 is on <b>M20</b> page 520 and <b>HDYDT?</b> page 42, consecrating Life Patterns with Prime 2 is also on <b>M20 </b>page 520 and <b>HDYDT?</b> page 46, and gravity manipulation isn't limited to Forces 4 and above - see Control Gravity on <b>Book of Common Magicks</b> page 20 for a Forces 2 version. The Forces 4 version is for large-scale Effects, as is normal for Forces 4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>\u200b<img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-thumb-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>\u200b\u200b<img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-thumb-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>\u200b<img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-thumb-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAPABAP///wAAACH5BAEKAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks - I would hope that it just clarifies how sympathy works with temporal scrying as well as spatial scrying and doesn't confuse people, but thanks for raising that point. It's worth keeping in mind for any future products.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, as I say, I disagree that most of the above are major shifts or additions but I do appreciate you taking the time to write out your feedback and I do take it in the spirit it's intended. I would hope that newcomers find it useful as I have tried to make it fit closely with M20 rules but of course it's not going to be for everyone. All the same, thank you very much for buying a copy - that is very cool.<br /> <br /> (<b>EDIT:</b> The only stuff that's genuinely new is one Effect in Prime (Obfuscation), taken from something similar in Mage: the Awakening. That's all. A few Effects are inferred from the existing Sphere descriptions: the stuff on fate and destiny in Entropy and the Unseen Aegis Effect in Matter, and I took inspiration from Awakening for some of these. Everything else comes from M20, supplemented by elements from Revised for detail. If folks think it would be helpful, I can update the product with a section that details this.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for taking these comments with good humor.<br /> <br /> Regarding absorbing quintessence: I don't believe this is the case. It is stated under the source provided that Prime 1 allows you to hold more quintessence than their avatar rating, but says nothing about absorbing quintessence.<br /> <br /> I see no mention of consecrating life patterns on Page 46, though M20 Page 520 does indeed mention concecration with life patterns, however, it does state specifically that it required Life 2 or Life 3 to do so, which your book does not mention.<br /> <br /> I have yet to do a full fact check on every aspect of the book as provided, but if you believe it would be helpful, I am happy to work with you to improve upon what is so far in place.<br /> <br /> What I would highly recommend is that the sources were included in the text so that they could be correctly attributed, and for effects in which either interpretations were made or decisions were made to change and wiggle them in to shape, that a discussion sidebar be included in order to explain the reasoning, either that such a thing was not properly elaborated on in M20 but was the case in Revised, or that something was interpreted from Awakening. If for no other reason than so readers can get a better idea on how these decisions were made, and can decide whether or not they too would come to the same conclusions or if they see them as departures to what they consider the game's default to be.<br /> <br /> I would also like to add that I am very interested in contributing to future iterations of this book, or similar such projects revolved around explaining, teaching, or providing examples detailing the logic of the spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-10-2023, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T15:24:03-08:00","id":1526634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault?p=1526625#post1526625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For clarity, you probably should.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And done <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T16:29:46-08:00","id":1526640,"title":"","content":"A minor suggestion: consider moving the Sources page to immediately follow Chapter Ten and to serve as the first page of the Appendix, to then be followed by the Sphere Summaries. I've made that change in my copy, and it flows a bit better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T17:51:38-08:00","id":1526643,"title":"","content":"Also: I noticed that in the Technocratic Spheres chapter, there's no mention of the Primal Utility \u2022\u2022\u2022 Effect \u201cCreate Stable Extraordinary Devices\u201d: it operates identically to the Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Effects \u201cEnchant Artifact\u201d and \u201cEnchant Talisman\u201d, but should still be listed separately because it's available through Primal Utility at Rank Three. <br /> <br /> You might also want to note that the Technocratic Spheres can get away with having more potent Effects because they also tend to <i>lack</i> Effects that their mystical counterparts have: Primal Utility doesn't have anything along the lines of Buzz, Body of Light, Rubbing the Bones, Primal Armor, or Primal Weapon, for instance. And Dimensional Science, while very good at manipulating the Gauntlet, is distinctly lacking in terms of ways to interact with EDEs (spirits): it has ways to detect them, attract then, and attack them, but lacks means to rouse or lull them, control them, create Fetishes, exorcise them, put them into people, or create them. Or, if they <i>can</i> do these things, there's no indication of it in any M20 book I'm aware of. This is less the case for Data; but that's largely because the difference between Correspondence and Data largely resides in which Correspondence Range Chart they use. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, you reproduced the Primal Ventures table from M20, but not the Data Connections table (p.524). Given that this tracks and how it works is central to how Data differs from Correspondence, that seems like a rather significant omission. <br /> <br /> (I would also note that <b>The Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick</b> lists a Prime \u2022 \u201cBank Run\u201d Rote that's essentially the same as the Primal Utility \u2022 \u201cExploit Primal Venture\u201d Effect, breaking the Syndicate's monopoly on Primal Ventures.)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T21:08:04-08:00","id":1526650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526391-book-of-common-magicks-released-on-st-vault?p=1526643#post1526643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: I noticed that in the Technocratic Spheres chapter, there's no mention of the Primal Utility \u2022\u2022\u2022 Effect \u201cCreate Stable Extraordinary Devices\u201d: it operates identically to the Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Effects \u201cEnchant Artifact\u201d and \u201cEnchant Talisman\u201d, but should still be listed separately because it's available through Primal Utility at Rank Three.<br /> <br /> You might also want to note that the Technocratic Spheres can get away with having more potent Effects because they also tend to <i>lack</i> Effects that their mystical counterparts have: Primal Utility doesn't have anything along the lines of Buzz, Body of Light, Rubbing the Bones, Primal Armor, or Primal Weapon, for instance. And Dimensional Science, while very good at manipulating the Gauntlet, is distinctly lacking in terms of ways to interact with EDEs (spirits): it has ways to detect them, attract then, and attack them, but lacks means to rouse or lull them, control them, create Fetishes, exorcise them, put them into people, or create them. Or, if they <i>can</i> do these things, there's no indication of it in any M20 book I'm aware of. This is less the case for Data; but that's largely because the difference between Correspondence and Data largely resides in which Correspondence Range Chart they use.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, you reproduced the Primal Ventures table from M20, but not the Data Connections table (p.524). Given that this tracks and how it works is central to how Data differs from Correspondence, that seems like a rather significant omission.<br /> <br /> (I would also note that <b>The Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick</b> lists a Prime \u2022 \u201cBank Run\u201d Rote that's essentially the same as the Primal Utility \u2022 \u201cExploit Primal Venture\u201d Effect, breaking the Syndicate's monopoly on Primal Ventures.)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Data chart was left out on purpose because there was only the one Data Effect listed that might reference it, as compared to several Primal Utility Effects needing their chart but it might be cool to just expand the entire chapter to give the Technocratic versions of every Effect for which there is an equivalent, even those that are basically just the same as mystick Effects under a different name. That could also allow me to capture a couple extra bits, like the Primal Utility Effects you mention, and Void Correspondence from the Revised Void Engineers book (which I was going to include and then decided against at the last minute). Thanks for your input - this is super helpful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T21:23:26-08:00","id":1526651,"title":"","content":"The reason to include the Data chart is that it's used by the Effects that Data inherits from Correspondence. The Data Connections table, <i>and the rules on how to use it, </i>would be important to Data even if there were <i>no </i>Effects exclusive to Data that use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T21:50:38-08:00","id":1526654,"title":"","content":"Yep, fair point. I think it would be a good addition when expanding this chapter. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxp